# Cloudflare Workers static assets are served *before* the Worker runs when a
# path matches a file, so the Worker's own header wrapping never executes for
# these. This file is the only thing that sets headers on them.
#
# All three matter, and none of them are optional:
#
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin
#   The view runs in a frame sandboxed without `allow-same-origin`, so its
#   document has an opaque origin and its own subresource fetches — CanvasKit,
#   the fonts — arrive as cross-origin requests with `Origin: null`.
#
# Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy
#   Lets those same subresources load when the embedder sets COEP.
#
# Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy
#   The host frame sets `require-corp`, and under that a nested *cross-origin
#   frame* must send COEP itself — CORP covers subresources, not documents.
#   Without it the browser refuses the frame outright with
#   ERR_BLOCKED_BY_RESPONSE, which the user sees as
#   "This content is blocked. Contact the site owner to fix the issue."

/app/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
